  "source": {
    "title": "Lurgan Mail, 21 September 1946, p. 5 (\"The Election: Independent Heads Poll\"; \"The Result with No. of Votes\")",
    "publisher": "Lurgan Mail (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "every figure read from the page image"
  },
  "note": "First election after the wartime postponement (the third elected in May 1939 had sat since then): the whole council of fifteen was elected at once, polled Wednesday 18 September 1946 and declared by W. R. Gracey, returning officer, on Thursday 19 September. Twenty-three candidates; 4,634 voted of an electorate of 6,242; 65 spoilt. Asterisk = retiring member. Labels as the paper gives them: Levin, Casey, Haughey and Beckett stood for the Labour Party; J. E. Johnston, McGrath, Fairley, Twyble, Ogle and Hopps were Official Unionist Party nominees; Magill, Monroe and Patterson were non-party; Liggett and Bridgett were put forward by the Lurgan \"A\" Branch of the British Legion. The unsuccessful candidates' labels are not given."
}
